  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Gusty thunderstorms are possible Wednesday \nafternoon and evening.\n\nUL trof progged to move across GL with corresponding SFC low\nmoving east Wed. WAA will prevail ahead of FROPA with gusty s'ly\nwinds. This will bring temps into the 70s areawide. Initial wave\nmay bring some showers, but LL dry air in place likely limits\nern extent. Second round of convection could be more robust\ngiven the background shear. There may be some storm\norganization. Given timing of tstorms near Alleghenies around\npeak heating, SPC has MRGL (Level 1 out of 5) for SVR WX on Wed.\nStorms should gradually weaken as they move east. Some models do\nhave a few tenths of QPF west of I-95 as storms diminish. The \nmain threat will be strong to locally damaging winds.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...After another cool down, above average \ntemperatures return for the weekend into early next week.\n\nCooler Thu with ULL over NE. Some residual upslope rain showers\nduring the day, with low probs of a shower E of the mtns. \n\nHigh pres builds overhead Fri which marks the start of the warm\nup. UL ridging continues to build in through the weekend. Highs\nby Sat & Sun likely widespread 80s (outside terrain) with low\n90s possible by Sun. SW may bring shower and tstorm potential \nat some point between Sat and Sun, but low confidence. Drier air\nmoves into the region at the start of next week as upper level \nridging builds, minimizing additional rain chances.",
